    arsenalScatterCaption:"Spatial scatter of the identified pass origins. Each point represents one record; some points may be close together or overlap.",
    arsenalHeatCaption:"Absolute frequency by area (6 × 5 grid). The highest-intensity cell contains 8 of the 34 records.",
    arsenalCaseResultsInterpretation:"The second half accounts for 23 of the 34 records (67.6%), compared with 11 (32.4%) in the first half. The spatial distribution is uneven: the most frequent area contains 8 passes in an advanced sector, while two nearby cells each contain 5 records. The visualisation should be read as the origin of the pass, not its destination or the location of the shot.",
    arsenalCaseInterpretationTitle:"05 · Football interpretation",
    arsenalCaseInterpretation1:"The map shows that the passes meeting the criteria originate more frequently in advanced areas of the pitch, particularly within the approximate longitudinal interval X=80–100. The most frequent cell contains 8 records (23.5% of the sample), while two other cells each contain 5 records (14.7%). These are recurring pass-origin areas within sequences that ended with a shot in the same possession.",
    arsenalCaseInterpretation2:"The distribution is consistent with Liverpool having a notable presence in the opposition half before some attempts, and suggests a question for video analysis: how are actions generated and connected from these advanced areas, who receives the ball, and what happens after the pass? Without additional information on destinations, receivers, progression, opposition pressure and shot quality, it cannot be concluded that these areas are the most effective or that the passes caused higher-value chances.",
    arsenalCaseInterpretation3:"The higher volume in the second half means that more records met the temporal and possession criteria during that period. It does not, by itself, demonstrate an increase in dominance, attacking intensity or chance quality. Such claims would require comparison with total possessions, shots, xG and match context.",
    arsenalCaseAuditTitle:"06 · Data audit and consistency",
